    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's just what people say to be nice, isn't it? to make it sound like there's always a light at the end of the tunnel. but i've lived through so much, and every time i try to \"work through it,\" it just gets harder. it's not just a feeling, it's like my actual foundation is gone. how can anyone be \"fixed\" when the core of them is just destroyed?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is understandable why you feel this way, as platitudes often fall flat when the pain is this deep. However, \"fixing\" someone often isn't about returning to how they were, but about building something new and resilient *around* the damage. Therapy can help you find ways to manage the intense core pain and build a new sense of self, even if the old foundations are gone. You don't have to \"fix\" everything at once; the goal can simply be to find support for the struggle itself.",
      "source": "target",
